    {
      "section_id": "SEC066",
      "title": "The A Part and the B Part",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Our trouble is that we read the warning passages of Scripture without also reading the promises that stand beside them. There is what might be called the B part of a text — its warnings — and there is the A part — its promise of life. To live is Christ; whatever a person might otherwise be living under, you cannot live in Christ and remain under the curse that these warnings describe.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA266",
            "REF056",
            "SRC007553",
            "SRC007557",
            "SRC007559",
            "SRC007560",
            "SRC007562"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC007553",
            "SRC007557",
            "SRC007559",
            "SRC007560",
            "SRC007562"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA266"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [
            "REF056"
          ],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000023",
          "provider_handle": "p23"
        },
        {
          "text": "Deuteronomy 30:19 sets this choice plainly: I put that choice before you, choose life. The same structure appears already in Deuteronomy 13.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "REF055",
            "REF052",
            "SRC007411",
            "SRC007412",
            "SRC007292",
            "SRC007294"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC007411",
